---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="Privacy & cookies | Ryan Hipkiss" />
	</head>
	<body>
		<section class="blog-header">
			<h1>Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
			<small>Last updated 9th October, 2026</small>
			<hr>
		</section>
		<section class="blog-content">
			<p>This is the personal website of Ryan Hipkiss. I'm responsible for any personal data collected through it. If you have a question about this notice, email <a href="mailto:ryan@ryanhipkiss.co.uk">ryan@ryanhipkiss.co.uk</a>.</p>

			<h2>Analytics cookies (only with your consent)</h2>
			<p>If you click <em>Accept</em> on the cookie banner, this site loads Google Analytics, provided by Google Ireland Limited. It sets the cookies <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_CQT66HFK83</code>, which last up to 2 years, and tells me which pages are visited, how visitors arrived, roughly where they are (country or city), and what device and browser they use. I use this only to understand which content people read. Google may process this data outside the UK, including in the United States.</p>
			<p>The lawful basis for this is your consent. If you click <em>Reject</em>, or don't make a choice, Google Analytics isn't loaded and no analytics cookies are set. Analytics data is kept for no more than 14 months.</p>

			<h2>Remembering your choice</h2>
			<p>Your cookie choice is saved in your browser's local storage under <code>cookie-consent</code>, so you aren't asked on every page. It never leaves your device.</p>

			<h2>Hosting</h2>
			<p>This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may log your IP address when you visit, for security purposes. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</p>

			<h2>Changing your mind</h2>
			<p><a href="/privacy/" data-cookie-settings>Change your cookie settings</a> at any time. If you withdraw consent, analytics stops and the analytics cookies are deleted.</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to access, correct or delete your personal data, or object to how it's used. Email me to do this. If you're unhappy with how your data has been handled, you can complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.</p>

			<a href="/" class="home-link">Go Back</a>
		</section>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
